{
  "duration": 75.199,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.039,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.74,
      "end": 3.419,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.819,
      "end": 7.479,
      "text": "Now in this problem, we are given that a train is traveling at seventy-two kilometer per hour,"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.98,
      "end": 9.88,
      "text": "and it crosses a pole in fifteen seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.519,
      "end": 13.279,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the length of the train."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.599,
      "end": 16.119,
      "text": "Now, the important words here are \"crosses a pole.\""
    },
    {
      "start": 16.859,
      "end": 17.979,
      "text": "What does this actually mean?"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.579,
      "end": 20.0,
      "text": "A pole has almost no width."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.359,
      "end": 21.719,
      "text": "So when a train crosses a pole,"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.1,
      "end": 24.339,
      "text": "the train covers only its own length."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.799,
      "end": 26.559,
      "text": "This is a simple rule to remember."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.399,
      "end": 28.759,
      "text": "When a train crosses a pole,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.399,
      "end": 32.02,
      "text": "distance covered equals length of the train."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.5,
      "end": 32.759,
      "text": "Done?"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.299,
      "end": 33.639,
      "text": "Great."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.239,
      "end": 35.68,
      "text": "Now, before using the formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.099,
      "end": 37.459,
      "text": "we should notice one more thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.059,
      "end": 40.159,
      "text": "The speed is given in kilometer per hour,"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.799,
      "end": 42.579,
      "text": "but the time is given in seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.059,
      "end": 46.579,
      "text": "So first, we must convert the speed into meter per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.939,
      "end": 51.959,
      "text": "We know seventy-two multiplied by five divided by eighteen is equal to twenty meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.319,
      "end": 53.239,
      "text": "Now this part is done."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.719,
      "end": 55.599,
      "text": "We can use this value in the next step."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.0,
      "end": 59.719,
      "text": "We know distance equals speed multiplied by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.259,
      "end": 65.22,
      "text": "Since the distance covered is the length of the train, length equals twenty multiplied by fifteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.779,
      "end": 67.959,
      "text": "After multiplying, we get three hundred meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.699,
      "end": 69.159,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.699,
      "end": 73.099,
      "text": "the length of the train is three hundred meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.519,
      "end": 75.199,
      "text": "So the final answer will be option D."
    }
  ],
